title: ch3_banker_review
---
Ms. Lee: Two locations now. Congratulations. Let me ask the question nobody asks. How many months could you survive with zero sales? #line:ch3_banker_review_01
-> Move a thousand dollars into the reserve today. #line:ch3_banker_review_02
    <<choose "reserve">>
    Ms. Lee: That's how I know who to lend to. The ones who don't need it tomorrow. #line:ch3_banker_review_03
-> Every dollar goes into growth. #line:ch3_banker_review_04
    <<choose "growth">>
    Ms. Lee: Growth is great until the first bad month. Keep my number close. #line:ch3_banker_review_05
===

title: ch3_rosa_contract
---
Rosa: You're buying for two places now. Sign a twelve-month contract and I'll drop my prices eight percent. #line:ch3_rosa_contract_01
Rosa: But a contract is a contract. Even in a slow month. #line:ch3_rosa_contract_02
-> Sign the contract. #line:ch3_rosa_contract_03
    <<choose "sign">>
    Rosa: Pleasure. First invoice comes with a free bag of something good. #line:ch3_rosa_contract_04
-> Stay flexible, buy month to month. #line:ch3_rosa_contract_05
    <<choose "flexible">>
    Rosa: Flexible costs extra. Your choice. #line:ch3_rosa_contract_06
===

title: ch3_mia_feature
---
Mia: A citywide outlet picked up my story about you. They want numbers. Real ones, or the shiny ones? #line:ch3_mia_feature_01
-> Give her the real numbers. #line:ch3_mia_feature_02
    <<choose "real">>
    Mia: The comments love you. Turns out people trust a founder who admits a bad month. #line:ch3_mia_feature_03
-> Round everything up a little. #line:ch3_mia_feature_04
    <<choose "shiny">>
    The article glows. A competitor's accountant starts doing math. #line:ch3_mia_feature_05
===

title: ch3_sam_equity
---
Sam: I've been helping on weekends for months. I want to go full time, for thirty percent of the company. #line:ch3_sam_equity_01
Unpaid CEO: Equity is forever. Founders usually vest it over four years with a one-year cliff. #line:ch3_sam_equity_02
-> Offer thirty percent, vesting over four years. #line:ch3_sam_equity_03
    <<choose "vesting">>
    Sam: Fair and smart. If I quit in six months, I shouldn't own a third. Deal. #line:ch3_sam_equity_04
-> Offer a salary instead of equity. #line:ch3_sam_equity_05
    <<choose "salary">>
    Sam: A job, not a company. I'll take it for now. #line:ch3_sam_equity_06
-> Say no. You'll stay the only owner. #line:ch3_sam_equity_07
    <<choose "no">>
    Sam: Then I'll build my own. No hard feelings. Mostly. #line:ch3_sam_equity_08
===

title: ch3_night_market
---
The Queens Night Market in Flushing Meadows has an open vendor spot this Saturday. #line:ch3_night_market_01
-> Set up a stall and stay until midnight. #line:ch3_night_market_02
    <<choose "go">>
    Ten thousand people, forty languages, one very long night. #line:ch3_night_market_03
-> Take the night off. #line:ch3_night_market_04
    <<choose "rest">>
    You walk through it as a customer. Dumplings taste better when you're not selling. #line:ch3_night_market_05
===

title: ch3_burnout
---
Jay: When did you last take a day off? Don't answer. I can see it on your face. #line:ch3_burnout_01
-> Take a full week off. The team covers. #line:ch3_burnout_02
    <<choose "break">>
    Jay: Look at that. The business survived without you. That's called a business. #line:ch3_burnout_03
-> Push through one more month. #line:ch3_burnout_04
    <<choose "push">>
    Jay: One more month. That's what you said last month. #line:ch3_burnout_05
===

title: boss_fatcat_poach
---
Your two best people come in together. Mr. Whiskerton offered them twenty percent more to switch. #line:boss_fatcat_poach_01
Mr. Whiskerton: Nothing personal. I just hire the best. You trained them so nicely. #line:boss_fatcat_poach_02
-> Match the offer with a raise. #line:boss_fatcat_poach_03
    <<choose "raise">>
    They stay. Payroll grows, and so does their loyalty. #line:boss_fatcat_poach_04
-> Refuse. Nobody gets a raise for a threat. #line:boss_fatcat_poach_05
    <<choose "refuse">>
    Two empty stations on Monday. The rest of the team noticed. #line:boss_fatcat_poach_06
-> Talk about growth paths, offer a smaller raise. #line:boss_fatcat_poach_07
    <<choose "talk">>
    One stays for the future you described. One leaves for the money. #line:boss_fatcat_poach_08
===
